From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:50:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a tooltip fits on the monitor it is on

On a tty with several monitors, a native tooltip (an <img title>) on a
monitor other than the host's opened far from the pointer and across two
monitors.

`TooltipAura::GetTooltipBounds` fits a tooltip in the display nearest its
anchor. The desk's host root holds the page's tooltips for every monitor
(0076), and its screen coordinates are the host's DIPs offset by its origin,
while `DrmScreen` lists displays in CRTC pixels. So the nearest display was
often another monitor, and the tooltip was moved onto that one's part of the
page.

The host's root now names each desk monitor in its own coordinates
(`kDomicileDeskMonitorsKey`, set by //chrome/browser/domicile), and a
tooltip fits in the one nearest its anchor.

Co-Authored-By: Connor Prussin <connor@prussin.net>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
